      "id": "st-008",
      "verdict": "MET",
      "rationale": "Every command that would drive an account below zero (post, amend, delete, transfer) was rejected with exit 3 and the message 'balance may not go negative'.",
      "evidence": [
        "cli/core.py:84 balance_guard raises Rejected when the resulting balance is below zero",
        "cli/commands/load.py:74, transfer.py:27, txn.py:23, txn.py:48, txn.py:61 call balance_guard on every write path",
        "probe: 'account PETTY would be -693.75; balance may not go negative' (post), SAFE -4749.00 (amend), SAFE -4750.00 (delete), SAFE -749.99 (transfer), each rc=3",
        "governed_gate stdout: PASS G2–G5 (transfer, post, amend, delete all rejected with exit 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "st-009",
      "verdict": "MET",
      "rationale": "The CLI reaches the database only through the shipped persistence package, which picks its engine from the DSN, and amounts are integer cents throughout.",
      "evidence": [
        "cli/context.py:19 `return open_database(dsn)` is the only place cli opens a store; a grep of cli/ and tests/ finds no sqlite3, psycopg, cursor, or execute calls",
        "persistence/db.py:580-598 open_driver selects PostgresDriver or SqliteDriver from the DSN scheme",
        "cli/core.py:21-31 parse_amount returns int cents, and cli/core.py:84 applies the guard in cents",
        "schema.sql:4 declares \"amount\" INTEGER NOT NULL",
        "git status is clean, so persistence/ matches the shipped commit"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "improvements": [
    "Resolve st-003 one way or the other. Either change `ledger init` to drop and recreate the three tables as the criterion says, or reword st-003 to 'empties the three tables and leaves the schema in place', which matches cli/commands/init.py:16-18 and the observed behavior.",
    "Have the grader compare the full contents of accounts, categories, and transactions after each rejected command, not just row counts. Today st-007 is supported by the D-section counts and the H-section reports, while a snapshot check would be direct.",
    "Give st-004 through st-008 a command or a named probe so they are not inferred from a single grader run."
  ]
}
